{
  "inShort": "At halfway, the vertical slice is at risk. The devlog claims a second island and reef damage, but shows a mountain photograph and a film thumbnail. No playable artifact landed, so what got done on the slice is unknown.",
  "discussed": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmvz5srg700w6p6z80zvvgym7",
      "text": "The repository opens and matches the task: public Godot demos with an MIT license and import instructions. It supplies a technical reference, not evidence of the game's tide loop or co-op sailing."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvz5srgy00w7p6z8tfpq30vg",
      "text": "The art reference remains done. Inspection reached only the Big Buck Bunny title and thumbnail, so the animation could not be verified. Reusing that link in the sprint devlog does not show the game's second island or reef damage."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvz5srhe00w8p6z89kwecilc",
      "text": "The playtesting article opens and matches the promised reading. It explains testing methods, but does not establish that five players tested the slice."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvz5srhu00w9p6z8yqrx4bpw",
      "text": "The private design board remains done through its existing artifact. No inspection result or new board evidence was supplied, so its contribution to the slice cannot be assessed."
    }
  ],
  "notDiscussed": [
    "cmvz5sriu00wap6p6z85ad7b4sk"
  ],
  "outsidePlan": [],
  "questions": [
    "Does an openable build contain both islands, the tide loop and two-player sailing?",
    "Have five players tested it, and what did their sessions reveal?",
    "Has the team chosen a visual style, beyond collecting a reference?"
  ],
  "lenses": {
    "marketing": "“Sprint 2: the second island, and the boat now takes damage on the reef” received 0 applause and 0 views; the project lists no store page or playable link.",
    "team": "The stated 10–15 hours weekly covers Alex only, leaving 20–30 stated hours for the remaining fortnight. Mia stopped confirming work this sprint, so her available programming time for the playable slice is unknown.",
    "management": "Four closed tasks establish references and planning, while no artifact closes the playable slice or five-player test. The published devlog meets the stage's sole exit requirement, but does not prove the working core and chosen style needed for a demo that can lead toward release."
  }
}

